Actually, the most logical thing for a player to do in a hopeless
situation (from an inside-the-game perspective) is to #quit. If you
quit, you get "You survived" as one of your attributes. Presumably all
adventurers who enter the dungeon are equipped with some sort of
last-resort signal flare, which they can set off to say, "Forget it! I
give up! I abandon the quest! Now get me out of here!"
Given this alternative, no person is really going to say, "Oh, looks
pretty hopeless down here, I could call on the gods of Nethack to get
me out of here and back out to the upper world, but instead I'll die
in an act of heroic self-sacrifice so that *somebody else* can succeed
where I failed and get that stupid Amulet..."

